# The Lighthouse at Gull Point: a short example gamebook.
@title The Lighthouse at Gull Point
@start gate

@passage gate
The keeper's gate creaks open onto a wet, grey headland.
A lantern glows in the tower above, and the path forks into the dunes.
- Take the cliff path to the tower -> tower_door
- Follow the dunes toward the wreck -> wreck
- Walk back to the village -> village_end

@passage tower_door
The tower door is locked. Someone has scratched a tide table into the wood.
- Read the tide table -> tide_clue
- Climb the rocks to the lamp-room window -> window
- Go back to the gate -> gate

@passage tide_clue
The table says the sea falls far enough to cross the sand at dusk.
- Wait for the tide to drop -> low_tide

@passage low_tide
Wet sand glitters in the last light. A sea cave yawns at the foot of the cliff.
- Walk across the sand to the sea cave -> cave

@passage cave
Inside, a brass key hangs from a nail beside a faded map.
- Take the brass key -> key

@passage key
The key turns in the lock. A spiral staircase climbs into the dark.
- Climb the stairs to the lamp room -> lamp_room

@passage window
The window is narrow, but you squeeze through and drop onto the lamp-room floor.
- Light the lamp -> lamp_room

@passage lamp_room ending
You light the lamp, and the beam sweeps across the bay. Far out, a ship turns for home.

@passage wreck
Timbers jut from the surf. Something is still tangled in the rigging.
- Swim out to the wreck -> storm_end
- Return to the gate -> gate

@passage storm_end ending
A cross-current takes you under before you reach the timbers. The tide keeps the rest of the story.

@passage village_end ending
You never learn what the light was for, but the fire in the inn is warm tonight.
